  {
   "id": "g-notes-programAdmissionRequirements",
   "label": "Program admission requirements",
   "category": "Major core",
   "sourceRef": "program",
   "rule": {
    "id": "r-notes-programAdmissionRequirements",
    "type": "review",
    "sourceRef": "program",
    "message": "Students must apply to the major. To apply, students must have completed, or be enrolled in, JOUR 1001 and have completed at least 12 graded credits (A-F). Students write answers to application questions that provide information about academic interests, professional goals, and mass communication or related experience, if any; the responses function as a writing sample for the Admissions Committee. The Admissions Committee is looking for a GPA of 3.0 or higher but will consider a GPA below 3.0 if grades have shown recent improvement. Verify this requirement with your advisor or APAS."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "g-notes-programRequirements",
   "label": "Additional program requirements",
   "category": "Liberal ed",
   "sourceRef": "program",
   "rule": {
    "id": "r-notes-programRequirements",
    "type": "review",
    "sourceRef": "program",
    "message": "All students must complete the University's\u00a0 Liberal Education requirements.\nCollegiate Requirements:\nAll CLA BA degrees require 18 upper-division (3xxx-level or higher) credits outside the major designator. These credits must be taken in designators different from the major designator and cannot include courses that are cross-listed with the major designator. The major designator for the Strategic Communication BA is JOUR.\nStudents are required to complete 4 semester(s) of any second language, with a grade of C-, or better, or S, or demonstrate proficiency in the language(s) as defined by the department or college.\nAll incoming CLA first-year (freshmen) must complete the First-Year Experience course sequence.\nAll incoming CLA first-year (freshmen) students earning a BA, BS, or BIS degree must complete CLA 3002 .or another approved career or internship course (CLA 3101, CLA 3201, CLA 3301, CLA 3896, or CLA 3996).\nAll students must complete a capstone in at least one CLA major. The requirements for double majors completing the capstone in a different CLA major will be clearly stated. Students must also complete all major requirements in both majors to allow the additional capstone to be waived. Students completing an additional degree must complete the Capstone in each degree area.\nAt least 17 upper-division credits in the major must be taken at the University of Minnesota Twin Cities campus.\nStudents may combine the Strategic Communication: Advertising and Public Relations BA with the Digital Media Studies minor, but not with the Media and Information minor.\nStudents may earn no more than one undergraduate major in Journalism, Strategic Communication: Advertising and Public Relations, and Media and Information. Verify this requirement with your advisor or APAS."
   }
  }
